mu0 needed so that 1/alpha_Y = 0 exactly at the Planck mass (the one free parameter, solved, not chosen):
  mu0 = 4.297186e+17 GeV  -> R / l_P = M_P/mu0 = 2.841138e+01 ; at that mu0 the check 1/alpha_Y(M_P) = 2.132e-14
  same with 1/alpha_Y(M_P) = 1 (bare unity in these units): mu0 = 4.369541e+17 GeV, R / l_P = 2.794092e+01

what the chain still needs: alpha_2. With 1/alpha_Y(Lambda) = 0 and sin^2 theta_W(Lambda) = 3/8 (alpha_Y/alpha_2 = 3/5) one gets 1/alpha_2(Lambda) = 0 as well (the ratio of two infinite couplings), which SU(2) cannot do because it is asymptotically free; the pair (alpha_Y, alpha_2) therefore needs a finite floor value or a separate input for alpha_2.

sensitivity of the solved R / l_P (hypercharge zero exactly at the Planck mass) to conventions and inputs:
  orbifold, one tower (b_tilde = 27/2)                 R / l_P = 28.411
  circle without orbifold (two towers, b_tilde x 2)    R / l_P = 15.190
  half the KK content (b_tilde x 1/2)                  R / l_P = 54.559
  1/alpha_Y(m_Z) shifted by -0.2%: R / l_P = 28.319
  1/alpha_Y(m_Z) shifted by +0.2%: R / l_P = 28.504
